# Mobile Development Standards

## Platform Specifics
- Target Platform: iOS (iPhone 16 Pro)
- Development: React Native CLI (not Expo)
- Future Support: All iOS devices and viewport sizes

## UI/UX Standards
### Visual Design
- Implement cyberpunk theme consistently
- Use approved color palette
- Maintain visual hierarchy
- Ensure readable typography

### Styling
```typescript
// Use StyleSheet.create for optimal performance
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    // Add comments for complex styles
  }
});
```

### Responsive Design
- Use relative units (%, flex) over fixed pixels
- Implement safe area handling
- Support dynamic text sizes
- Test on multiple device sizes

## Performance Optimization
### List Rendering
```typescript
<FlatList
  removeClippedSubviews={true}
  maxToRenderPerBatch={10}
  windowSize={5}
  getItemLayout={(data, index) => ({
    length: ITEM_HEIGHT,
    offset: ITEM_HEIGHT * index,
    index,
  })}
/>
```

### Asset Management
- Use react-native-fast-image for images
- Implement vector icons efficiently
- Optimize asset loading and caching
- Implement proper cleanup

## Logging Strategy
### Development
- Log important state changes
- Track performance metrics
- Monitor animation frames
- Debug network requests

### Production
- Remove development-only logs
- Maintain critical error logging
- Track key user interactions
- Monitor performance metrics

## Animation Guidelines
- Use native driver when possible
- Implement smooth transitions
- Optimize gesture handling
- Maintain 60fps target